    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432">

                <pb facs="0534" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg524"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/8–544</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Aviation Division</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Counselor of
                        the Belgian Embassy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cruben</hi>)<anchor n="67"
                        xml:id="d432-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-05">August 5, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Baron de Gruben</hi>: In anticipation of the
                    exploratory talks on aviation which are to commence next Monday,<anchor n="68"
                        xml:id="d432-f2"/> I take pleasure <pb facs="0535" n="525" xml:id="pg525"/>
                    in sending you herewith, for the information of the Belgian group who will
                    participate in these talks, a copy of a “Summary of Objectives Favored by the
                    United States of America With Respect to Post-War Civil Air Transport”.<anchor
                        n="69" xml:id="d432-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>This document has been submitted to the other national groups with whom we have
                    already held exploratory talks, as a basis for discussion and exchange of views.
                    This summary has been prepared tentatively, on a technical level, and is to be
                    considered as strictly informal.</p>
                <p>We will be happy to receive any statement of the views or objectives of the
                    Belgian Government that you care to submit for our consideration either before
                    or during the talks. We are looking forward with a great deal of pleasure to
                    this opportunity to exchange views with Belgium.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stokeley W. Morgan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d432-f1" n="67" type="source" xml:id="d432-f1-content">
                <p>A similar letter was sent on August 14 to the Indian Agency General with the
                    information that exploratory talks were set to commence on August 22.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d432-f2" n="68" xml:id="d432-f2-content">
                <p>August 7.</p>
            </note>
